  "query_preview": "..\nThe Marianas are on the far eastern periphery of a disorganized,\nunsettled pattern over Yap State, centered around Joint Typhoon \nWarning Center (JTWC)'s Invest 96W. 96W is currently located near \nYap Proper around 8N139E. A weak, shallow trough extends northeast \nfrom 96W to the west of the Marianas, and a second weak trough \nextends eastward from the disturbance, passing to the south of Guam. \nThe positioning of these features is steering moderate southeast \nwinds across the islands this afternoon, with patches of scattered \nshowers developing within the convergent flow east to southeast of \nGuam. Invest 96W will meander very slowly over the next day or so, \nstalling somewhere just north of Yap and maintaining a more unsettled\npattern for the Marianas through at least Wednesday night. On \nWednesday, gentle southeast winds may become light and variable at \ntimes, and allow for the development of scattered island showers over\nGuam in the afternoon, especially if skies clear by around mid day. \nA fairly dry pattern will set up by the end of the week, with a \nreturn to moderate to fresh trade winds this coming weekend.",
